  "question": {
    "text": "A tangent and a normal are drawn at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;which meet the directrix of the parabola at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is a point such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is a square, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math>",
